# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GANESH NURSERY — environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development, and put the same values in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for the live site.
#
# TWO KINDS OF VALUE, AND THE DIFFERENCE MATTERS
#
#   VITE_*    compiled into the JavaScript the browser downloads. Public.
#   others    only ever read on the server, inside /api. Never sent anywhere.
#
# DATABASE_URL and ADMIN_PASSWORD have no VITE_ prefix, and must never be
# given one. That prefix is the only thing standing between them and every
# visitor's developer tools.
#
# Full walkthrough: NEON-SETUP.md
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Database (Neon) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neon dashboard → Connect → copy the "Pooled connection" string.
# Server-side only. Without it the site still runs, serving the catalogue it
# shipped with, but nothing can be edited.
DATABASE_URL=

# ─── Admin password ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one password that opens /admin. Server-side only — it is never sent to
# the browser, which is why this is a real lock rather than the latch the old
# passphrase was.
#
# Use something long. Anyone with it can change the prices the public sees.
# Changing it here and redeploying signs everyone out.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ─── Photos (Cloudinary) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudinary → Dashboard for the cloud name; Settings → Upload for the preset.
# The preset must be set to "Unsigned".
#
# These two are public by design: they only allow uploading into one folder,
# and NEON-SETUP.md explains how to cap that.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=

# Optional. The folder uploads land in. Change it only if one Cloudinary
# account serves several sites.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_FOLDER=ganesh-nursery

# ─── Contact form ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. If set, the contact form POSTs enquiries here (Formspree,
# Web3Forms, a Google Apps Script — anything accepting JSON). If left empty
# the form falls back to opening WhatsApp with the message pre-filled, so an
# enquiry is never silently lost.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=
